# Rules for Javascript files and widgets

- Some widgets are located under protected/js, the protected folder will be deprecated, do not add files in this folder
- New js files should be added to gigadb/app/client/js folder and imported in php files as follows
```php
Yii::app()->assetManager->forceCopy = YII_DEBUG; // needed during development 
jsDir = Yii::getAlias('/gigadb/app/client/js/path-to-js-folder');
$jsUrl = Yii::app()->assetManager->publish($jsDir);
$jsPath = $jsUrl . '/filename.js';

Yii::app()->clientScript->registerScriptFile($jsPath, CClientScript::POS_END, ['type' => 'module']);

<script type="module">
  import { myJsFunction } from '<?php echo $jsPath; ?>';

  $(document).ready(function() {
    myJsFunction()
  });
</script>
```
- New js files should be structured as js modules
- Write JS using best coding practices and modern JS (ES6)
- Always use jquery 3 instead of JS DOM to interact with the DOM